.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_CTX_SET_STATELESS_COOKIE_GENERATE_CB 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_stateless_cookie_generate_cb ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_stateless_cookie_verify_cb ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_cookie_generate_cb ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_cookie_verify_cb
.Nd Callback functions for stateless TLS1.3 cookies
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_CTX_set_stateless_cookie_generate_cb
.Fa "      SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "int (*gen_stateless_cookie_cb) (SSL *ssl"
.Fa "unsigned char *cookie"
.Fa "size_t *cookie_len)"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_CTX_set_stateless_cookie_verify_cb
.Fa "      SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "int (*verify_stateless_cookie_cb) (SSL *ssl"
.Fa "const unsigned char *cookie"
.Fa "size_t cookie_len)"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_CTX_set_cookie_generate_cb
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "int (*app_gen_cookie_cb) (SSL *ssl"
.Fa "unsigned char                                                                *cookie"
.Fa "unsigned int                                                                *cookie_len)"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_CTX_set_cookie_verify_cb
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "int (*app_verify_cookie_cb) (SSL *ssl"
.Fa "const unsigned                                                                 char *cookie"
.Fa "unsigned int                                                                 cookie_len)"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_stateless_cookie_generate_cb
sets the callback used by
.Xr SSL_stateless 3
to generate the application-controlled portion of the cookie provided to
clients in the HelloRetryRequest transmitted as a response to a
ClientHello with a missing or invalid cookie.
.Xr gen_stateless_cookie_cb 3
must write at most SSL_COOKIE_LENGTH bytes into
.Fa cookie ,
and must write the number of bytes written to
.Sy cookie_len .
If a cookie cannot be generated, a zero return value can be used to
abort the handshake.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_stateless_cookie_verify_cb
sets the callback used by
.Xr SSL_stateless 3
to determine whether the application-controlled portion of a ClientHello
cookie is valid.
The cookie data is pointed to by
.Fa cookie
and is of length
.Sy cookie_len .
A nonzero return value from
.Xr verify_stateless_cookie_cb 3
communicates that the cookie is valid.
The integrity of the entire cookie, including the application-controlled
portion, is automatically verified by HMAC before
.Xr verify_stateless_cookie_cb 3
is called.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_cookie_generate_cb
sets the callback used by
.Xr DTLSv1_listen 3
to generate the cookie provided to clients in the HelloVerifyRequest
transmitted as a response to a ClientHello with a missing or invalid
cookie.
.Xr app_gen_cookie_cb 3
must write at most DTLS1_COOKIE_LENGTH bytes into
.Fa cookie ,
and must write the number of bytes written to
.Sy cookie_len .
If a cookie cannot be generated, a zero return value can be used to
abort the handshake.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_cookie_verify_cb
sets the callback used by
.Xr DTLSv1_listen 3
to determine whether the cookie in a ClientHello is valid.
The cookie data is pointed to by
.Fa cookie
and is of length
.Sy cookie_len .
A nonzero return value from
.Xr app_verify_cookie_cb 3
communicates that the cookie is valid.
The integrity of the cookie is not verified by OpenSSL. This is an
application responsibility.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Neither function returns a value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7 ,
.Xr SSL_stateless 3 ,
.Xr DTLSv1_listen 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_stateless_cookie_generate_cb
and
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_stateless_cookie_verify_cb
were added in OpenSSL 1.1.1.
